course: dictionary
lesson: 1593
title: Cheating and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cheating means acting dishonestly to win or to get an advantage. It means breaking the rules in secret. «Cheating, like peeking in hide-and-seek, spoils the game for everyone.» Peeking is a small rule-break, and it still spoils the fun, so cheating is about being unfair.
explain: Look at the clue words in this sentence: «Cheating is breaking the rules in secret to gain an unfair advantage.» Breaking the rules, in secret, and unfair advantage all tell you the meaning. Swap in your own meaning, "Copying answers is breaking the rules in secret to win," and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Cheating is also a verb, so you will see cheat, cheats, cheated and cheating. «Cheating» can name the act, as in «Cheating is wrong», or describe what someone is doing, as in «He was cheating at cards». Both uses point to the same idea: dishonest, unfair rule-breaking.
fact: Cheating means acting dishonestly to win or get an advantage.
fact: A «cheat sheet» is a secret note that someone uses in a test.
fact: «Cheat at» a game means breaking its rules, and «no cheating!» is what a teacher says before a test.
fact: Cheating is not only in tests: «a handball goal» and «a hidden motor in a bike» break the rules too, even when the referee does not see.
fact: Cheating spoils the fun, is unfair to others, and means nobody can see what you really know.
exercise: «Cheating is breaking the rules in secret to gain an unfair advantage.» What does advantage mean here? | A rule book | A hidden note | A game with no winners | *An edge that helps you win
exercise: Which of these is cheating in a game? | Helping a friend tie a shoelace | Sharing the dice fairly | *Moving extra squares when you are losing | Reading the rules before you play
exercise: Which phrase means a secret note used in a test? | cheat at a game | *cheat sheet | no cheating | handball goal
test: Mia says, «He cheated at the board game, so it wasn't fair.» What does cheated at mean here? | Forgot how to play | *Broke the rules to win | Played the game very well | Gave up halfway
test: Why is cheating on a test wrong? | It makes the teacher sad | It makes the test shorter | *It means the teacher cannot see what you really know | It is the fastest way to learn
exam: Jayden says cheating is fine if nobody sees it. Why is he wrong? | It is fine, because only the referee can judge | *It still breaks the rules and is unfair to others, even when no one sees | Nobody can ever prove cheating, so it does not count | Cheating is only bad in sport
